"bytes\": 6177,\n+      \"sha256\": \"98b7cf1fcfeb738af6b4d5faca0e990b6ed9f4cb58bc7492806879591e248a45\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"TURN_3_CHECKS.json\",\n+      \"bytes\": 649,\n+      \"sha256\": \"2eff1658244fda3eb2f16d64e42919e6b2e9f0cf6e53589377b7c600c2325cc6\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"TURN_3_MANIFEST.json\",\n+      \"bytes\": 934,\n+      \"sha256\": \"3c51a31e336be139fa8087a44392b567a48dd101eb601fe76ab9c46b0c1f8162\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"TURN_3_REMOTE_RECEIPT.json\",\n+      \"bytes\": 2766,\n+      \"sha256\": \"f25d6f340f88e69c25be2c05e90e9a6677b44db06c3d6215838eb7fdd12eac35\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"TURN_3_SURVIVORS.txt\",\n+      \"bytes\": 210,\n+      \"sha256\": \"4288f41ee220ebeb902514b301d701156d57ed6f7bfcbc2380be85af41325f52\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"TURN_4.md\",\n+      \"bytes\": 9579,\n+      \"sha256\": \"90a46e0ba1aee642bd5faedfbb89c94c316d128b46b24e297e355050fabb0cf5\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"TURN_4_CHECKS.json\",\n+      \"bytes\": 574,\n+      \"sha256\": \"d541bfc16409de3b4c4e171e590c809aca6456a164a5a4a7dcb5680185c0820b\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"TURN_4_CPP_CHECKS.json\",\n+      \"bytes\": 514,\n+      \"sha256\": \"661ef52ff67574e217c270b60ddededdd76799c8904e49e31006d4b25918fd54\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"TURN_4_MANIFEST.json\",\n+      \"bytes\": 1242,\n+      \"sha256\": \"5ea770b400070f25af6206459e03eccfd58db95355a05968c0c0af96c43b7dae\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"check_turn_1.py\",\n+      \"bytes\": 2957,\n+      \"sha256\": \"68751e5a701247344c32517aea0752711175c3e72c50fda0a5e93445db78db5c\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"check_turn_2.py\",\n+      \"bytes\": 2121,\n+      \"sha256\": \"a0385e57064caf3353007b20f374361720544dd7067590dd81d7b3b3d092f2a5\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"check_turn_3.py\",\n+      \"bytes\": 2685,\n+      \"sha256\": \"c6de7525ee866f4e384e36983f4ba17281b6d463bf1a9bb32fdc85966ad7a2bf\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"check_turn_4.cpp\",\n+      \"bytes\": 5114,\n+      \"sha256\": \"7ca50a2a0804b592b741f2fc04e3a2178101eabcf8a23aa262cdabd95e110843\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"check_turn_4.py\",\n+      \"bytes\": 2665,\n+      \"sha256\": \"37adab4df9e3efa67ef934b5c0006957de7ded4001b3eb8bdcd555c26b55f17e\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"verify_turn_4_cpp.py\",\n+      \"bytes\": 1213,\n+      \"sha256\": \"b8e1f2e6ca69699cccbfc353bd1361c15d9f0faf2fa56905ed3ea85f71cc7243\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}"},{"sha":"80729c6ce8658534f8e849dc5d8e9e8c6ee33a89","filename":"problems/11000151_artin_a5_quotient/FINAL_README.md","status":"added","additions":7,"deletions":0,"changes":7,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/d977c9564f079cde975a7b4261776eb9061c5f5f/problems%2F11000151_artin_a5_quotient%2FFINAL_README.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/d977c9564f079cde975a7b4261776eb9061c5f5f/problems%2F11000151_artin_a5_quotient%2FFINAL_README.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/problems%2F11000151_artin_a5_quotient%2FFINAL_README.md?ref=d977c9564f079cde975a7b4261776eb9061c5f5f","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@\n+# Reproduction\n+\n+Run check_turn_1.py, check_turn_2.py, check_turn_3.py and check_turn_4.py using Python's standard library. Compare complete stdout to TURN_n_CHECKS.json. The second checker reuses the first's exact free-group functions. The third generates the ten-line survivor list if absent and otherwise verifies its exact bytes.\n+\n+Then run verify_turn_4_cpp.py with an installed g++ supporting C++17. It compiles the second exact implementation in a temporary directory, hashes its full state-action stream and compares it with the Python receipt. No large stream file is retained. Running the compiled checker with --stream regenerates the complete90921-record certificate. Both programs compare full reduced words before hashing.\n+\n+Read the written completeness proof and source scope; finite computations alone do not replace the classical topological and braid-group inputs. No external group solver or downloaded executable is used. Raw source files and exploratory work are not public artifacts. Earlier frozen proof/checker bytes are preserved."},{"sha":"bd900bcc40b58f581fd9d3109d83669e5aac01da","filename":"problems/11000151_artin_a5_quotient/FINAL_RESULT.md","status":"added","additions":11,"deletions":0,"changes":11,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/d977c9564f079cde975a7b4261776eb9061c5f5f/problems%2F11000151_artin_a5_quotient%2FFINAL_RESULT.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/d977c9564f079cde975a7b4261776eb9061c5f5f/problems%2F11000151_artin_a5_quotient%2FFINAL_RESULT.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/problems%2F11000151_artin_a5_quotient%2FFINAL_RESULT.md?ref=d977c9564f079cde975a7b4261776eb9061c5f5f","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+# Complete convention-qualified classification candidate at4/5\n+\n+For the exact quotientG ofB6 by c=h, with c=(a1a2a3a4)^5 and h=a5a4a3a2 a1² a2a3a4a5, classify positive words in the five fixed standard generators representing c².\n+\n+The possible lengths are exactly20,30,40. There is one strict Hurwitz class at20, one at30, and two at40. The40-letter classes are represented by the full-twist squares on the first five and last five strands. They are distinguished by their generated subgroups inS6 and are identified by simultaneous conjugation.\n+\n+Thus the requested three standard representatives give the complete classification after simultaneous conjugation. Under strict Hurwitz moves alone the literal single40-class clause fails, and the corrected complete list has four classes. Wajnryb's brief wording does not definitively distinguish the conventions; both answers are supplied. This is not a classification of arbitrary factors conjugate to generators or arbitrary nonseparating twists.\n+\n+Dependencies: the credited Baykur–Monden–Van Horn-Morris maximum40, classical chain relations/Perron–Vannier injection, pure-braid linking, faithful Artin action and Garside positive-monoid embedding. The twenty-letter case reduces exhaustively to810 words, of which exactly ten central cyclic rotations survive a necessary quotient representation test. The thirty-letter case uses a complete finite crossing-state DAG with261810 exact free-group-action edge comparisons. Python and C++ agree on all90921 coaccessible state actions and the full stream digest. Finite reductions and source hypotheses are proved in the turn files; no graph sample is extrapolated.\n+\n+Four genuine turns completed. Author search stopped at the complete candidate; full independent review is required before disposition or publication. No novelty certification. Earlier frozen partial snapshots remain unchanged."},{"sha":"1491e0073b5394e58063204f51e8568181daa20a","filename":"problems/11000151_artin_a5_quotient/FINAL_REVIEW_REQUEST.md","status":"added","additions":17,"deletions":0,"changes":17,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/d977c9564f079cde975a7b4261776eb9061c5f5f/problems%2F11000151_artin_a5_quotient%2FFINAL_REVIEW_REQUEST.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/d977c9564f079cde975a7b4261776eb9061c5f5f/problems%2F11000151_artin_a5_quotient%2FFINAL_REVIEW_REQUEST.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/problems%2F11000151_artin_a5_quotient%2FFINAL_REVIEW_REQUEST.md?ref=d977c9564f079cde975a7b4261776eb9061c5f5f","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@\n+# Full independent review request\n+\n+Read SOURCE_GATE.md and all four TURN_n.md files, then FINAL_RESULT.md. Exact original page: source/mcgbook.pdf physical133/printed126, with complete Wajnryb chapter printed122–128 and Auroux's conventions printed131–132. Raw sources stay outside public packet.\n+\n+High-risk obligations:\n+\n+1. Fixed-generator positive words are the quantified objects; distinguish arbitrary conjugate-twist factorizations. Wajnryb does not define his own equivalence convention. Check both the strict-four-class and modulo-global-conjugation-three-class conclusions, without silently deciding the intended convention.\n+2. Geometric map from the exact quotient: full-twist identityz=ch plus both chain relations givesc=h after capping one boundary. Nonseparating curves and genus2/one-boundary hypotheses match the published maximum40. No quotient injection is assumed for that bound.\n+3. Normal-closure linking vectors: signed arbitrary conjugates of the pure relator yield six vertex patterns. Positivity and integer inequalities exclude0/10 and classify the allowed linking vectors without bounding the conjugate counts.\n+4. Forty-letter slice: no crossing of an isolated strand forces it to an endpoint; Perron–Vannier applies to the four-chain regular neighborhood after capping. Positive monoid embedding and the explicit two Hurwitz moves implement braid relations. Check the subgroup invariant distinguishing the two strong classes.\n+5. Twenty-letter slice: all810 center-strand walks must be exhaustive. Verify every inverse, braid relation and c=h in the Aut(F4) table. The action is only a necessary rejection test; all ten survivors must have directG-certificates as cyclic rotations ofh², not be accepted on an unproved faithful quotient representation.\n+6. Thirty-letter slice: crossing-count parity determines permutation; merging loses no available continuation. Verify the complement-reachability/coaccessibility criterion carefully: reverse positive words, not braid inverses. Every complete path lies in the coaccessible DAG. Exact action equality on every edge implies equality on every path by induction. The Artin free-group action is faithful, with the explicitly explained inverse-generator/right-action convention. All261810 edges are tested, with no cap or hash-only equality assumption.\n+7. Replay all four Python checkers and the C++ wrapper. Check frozen earlier manifests, final manifest, raw source bindings and immutable remote blobs. The large action stream is regenerable, not retained. Do not turn its digest into a claim of stored full certificate bytes.\n+\n+Source dependencies: published Baykur–Monden–Van Horn-Morris TheoremA1529; corresponding genus2 proof in arXivv2; Wajnryb source Theorem2.1 and chain relations; González-Meneses §§1.6 and4, printed22–24 and42–44. No source PDFs/imports/exploratory directories should be published.\n+\n+Four turns are complete and frozen; no fifth author search unless a mandatory review correction genuinely requires it. Return exact mandatory corrections or a full qualified PASS. No publication before the gate."},{"sha":"1af3ea448a51c75b9b7b6069c8c8051186096b76","filename":"problems/11000151_artin_a5_quotient/PUBLICATION_MANIFEST.json","status":"added","additions":217,"deletions":0,"changes":217,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/d977c9564f079cde975a7b4261776eb9061c5f5f/problems%2F11000151_artin_a5_quotient%2FPUBLICATION_MANIFEST.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/d977c9564f079cde975a7b4261776eb9061c5f5f/problems%2F11000151_artin_a5_quotient%2FPUBLICATION_MANIFEST.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/problems%2F11000151_artin_a5_quotient%2FPUBLICATION_MANIFEST.json?ref=d977c9564f079cde975a7b4261776eb9061c5f5f","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,217 @@\n+{\n+  \"problem_id\": 11000151,\n+  \"status\": \"claimed_solved\",\n+  \"turns\": 4,\n+  \"files\": [\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"FINAL_AUTHOR_MANIFEST.json\",\n+      \"bytes\": 5131,\n+      \"sha256\": \"dc4840da287b2d44fab7fa0eea0a66a2f617b98e6f953a76dd917dd7adcbafac\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"FINAL_README.md\",\n+      \"bytes\": 1054,\n+      \"sha256\": \"d09e0c8c3d1f478b76945c8f473ca939d823e1aaeeaf472808f57ae665b90d6f\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"FINAL_RESULT.md\",\n+      \"bytes\": 1896,\n+      \"sha256\": \"1af44af62694882e032a16bad65e7d816e5